  "system_description": {
    "narrative_title": "Middle East chokepoints and Houthi attacks driving a global oil shock",
    "narrative_summary": "A cascade of Houthi advances in the Red Sea and repeated strikes on Gulf infrastructure has tightened physical oil and shipping flows through critical chokepoints (Bab al-Mandeb, Strait of Hormuz). That disruption propagates through the open system of production, refining, tanker logistics, and futures markets to lift crude and diesel prices, spike tanker rates, and feed consumer inflation — prompting policy, military and industrial responses. Feedbacks include supply losses -> higher prices -> political/economic countermeasures (pipeline shutdowns, defence postures, refinery measures) that can either mitigate or further exacerbate disruptions.",
    "scope": "The system boundary covers the global oil supply chain and price-formation system as affected by Middle East maritime security: production/export infrastructure, shipping lanes and chokepoints (Hormuz, Bab al-Mandeb), tanker logistics and freight rates, inventories and refining capacity, futures/spot markets, and downstream consumer fuel prices and economic demand.",
    "super_system": "Global energy–economic–financial system (global trade, commodity markets, macroeconomy and geopolitical stability).",
    "adjacent_subsystems": [
      "Maritime security and naval/military operations in the Red Sea and Persian Gulf",
      "Global shipping and logistics (tanker markets, freight rates, insurance)",
      "Domestic inflation and transport/industrial fuel demand",
      "International diplomacy and regional security arrangements (Iran, Gulf states, Pakistan, US)"
    ],
    "evidence_headlines": [
      "Iran-backed Houthis seize key port in Yemen, advance on another vital oil choke point",
      "Saudi Arabia shuts East-West pipeline that bypasses Hormuz after attacks",
      "U.S. diesel price tops $6 per gallon, a record high as Ukraine and Iran wars ripple through economy",
      "IEA warns 2026 oil supply gap will widen on delayed return of normal Gulf flows - reuters.com",
      "Oil tanker rates hit record highs following Iran, US shipping attacks"
    ]
  },
